---
import Next from '../components/Next.astro'
import Snippet from '../components/Snippet.astro'
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
---

<Page
  page="document"
  title="Document"
  description="Markdown beside every operation, or Try it on any button of your existing documentation site, in your own theme."
>
  <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 24px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">02 · Document</span>
      <h1 class="display">Docs that run.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Write markdown beside every operation, or add Try it to any button on your existing documentation site.
        Readers send real requests without leaving the page, in your theme.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" style="padding-top: 8px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="title">Write notes beside each operation</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Drop a Markdown file right next to the endpoint it describes.</p>
      </div>
      <Snippet file="demo/requests/petstore/GetPetById/README.md" region="notes" title="requests/petstore/GetPetById/README.md" />
      <div class="demo">
        <div class="demo-bar">
          <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          <span>What a reader sees</span>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-body prose" style="max-width: none">
          <p>
            <button type="button" data-specbook-try="petstore/GetPetById" data-specbook-env="mock" data-specbook-tab="docs">
              Open the docs for Get a pet by id
            </button>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <details class="more">
          <summary>Where your notes live</summary>
          <ul>
            <li>An operation: a <code>README.md</code> in its folder, like <code>requests/petstore/GetPetById/README.md</code>.</li>
            <li>Or one file per operation in the service's <code>docs</code> folder, like <code>requests/petstore/docs/GetPetById.md</code>.</li>
            <li>A request: <code>&lt;name&gt;.req.md</code> beside <code>&lt;name&gt;.req.ts</code>.</li>
            <li>A flow: <code>&lt;name&gt;.seq.md</code> beside <code>&lt;name&gt;.seq.ts</code>.</li>
            <li>Anywhere else: a markdown file whose front matter names what it documents, like <code>operation: petstore/GetPetById</code>.</li>
            <li>A field: a heading made of one code span, like <code>## `petId`</code>, attaches its text to that field.</li>
          </ul>
        </details>
      </div>

      <h2 class="title">Make any example runnable</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Load one script on your documentation site and add a data attribute. A plain element gets a Play
          button beside it, and a button or link that carries the attribute opens the panel itself.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Snippet file="snippets/embed.html" region="embed" title="docs.html" />
      <div class="demo">
        <div class="demo-bar">
          <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          <span>On this page, it does this</span>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-body prose" style="max-width: none">
          <p data-specbook-try="requests/petstore/get-pet.req.ts" data-specbook-env="mock">
            Fetch a pet by its id and see the response checked against the spec.
          </p>
          <p style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px">
            <button type="button" data-specbook-flow="new-pet" data-specbook-env="mock">
              Register a pet with a generated name
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              data-specbook-flow="adopt-pet"
              data-specbook-env="mock"
              data-specbook-inputs='{"quantity":2}'
            >
              Adopt two pets
            </button>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="title">It looks like your site</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The panel is isolated from your page, so neither can break the other. It uses your colors, follows your
          light or dark theme as it changes, and keeps what a visitor types out of your storage. Every attribute
          and variable is in the <a href="/reference/embed/">reference</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Snippet file="snippets/theme.css" region="theme" title="site.css" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap"><Next page="document" /></div>
</Page>
